Ghost-name pool
---------------
The matchmaking server uses a curated pool of player handles and aliases. The runtime list contains names only; this notice carries the source records. The pool combines sources with different terms, so no single license is asserted for the entire pool.

Liquipedia-derived aliases are attributed to Liquipedia contributors and licensed under CC BY-SA 3.0. This selection has been filtered against the server's name policy and deduplicated; these are modifications to the sourced material. The Liquipedia-derived portion remains available under CC BY-SA 3.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/ . API terms: https://liquipedia.net/api-terms-of-use .

The Steam sample comes from the nyuuzyou/steambans dataset, marked CC0 1.0: https://huggingface.co/datasets/nyuuzyou/steambans .

OpenDota's pro-player API is recorded as a source, but its reviewed API documentation does not state a license for returned data. OpenDota's MIT code license is not treated as a data license: https://docs.opendota.com/ and https://api.opendota.com/api/proPlayers . The retained legacy set has no source or license record in the repository.

SAHA's public site displays "All rights reserved" and no separate reuse license was found in the reviewed pages. Its source links are retained below as attribution, not as permission to reuse. The same applies to the listed individual creator pages unless their owners grant permission. This notice does not claim those sources are cleared for reuse: https://saha.gg/leaderboard .

